  body: "# Personal rate of JSA(Cont) in the DMG\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured chapter
    describes JSA(Cont) as paid for the claimant alone, without increases for a partner or dependants,
    and distinguishes its personal rate from the JSA(IB) applicable amount.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\
    \nThis is the frozen DMG JSA(Cont) context. It does not establish current New Style JSA rules, current
    rates or entitlement. Earnings and pension deductions and the comparison where both sets of conditions
    are satisfied require their own review; numerical examples are historical source examples.\n\n## Inspected
    source passages\n\n- [DMG 23007, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f95b98c6c9802f7ed9c7/dmg-Ch-23.pdf#page=3)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 23: Normal amount payable.\n- [DMG 23015, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f95b98c6c9802f7ed9c7/dmg-Ch-23.pdf#page=6)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 23: Normal amount payable.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol4-ch23`: PDF SHA-256 `174fce491e7a72ca89f2739a64ab4e2f3a0da6e33d9e48eaa5c33c7ff9a5f734`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `387302f09bbce9873dbafcd6af6a19b06842b35392e7d7771058ed22a0bd8bd2`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-applicable-amount
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source compares the personal rate and applicable amount when both conditions of
      entitlement are satisfied; the association does not add the two amounts or calculate an award.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch23/0006
      quote: "23015 Where a claimant satisfies both the JSA(Cont) and JSA(IB) conditions of entitlement
        and has no\nincome, the amount payable is\n\n\n1. the applicable amount, if it is greater than
        the personal rate or\n\n\n2. if 1. does not apply, the personal rate1.\n\n\n                 \
        \                                                                         1 JS Act 95, s 4(6)"
      locator: DMG 23015
  - target: term/jsais-gross-employed-earnings
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The personal-rate passage expressly identifies earnings as a deduction and routes
      employed-earnings research to chapter 26.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch23/0003
      quote: "23007 JSA(Cont) is paid for the claimant only. There are no increases for any partner or
        dependants. The\n\npersonal rate is calculated by1\n\n\n1. deciding the age-related amount payable
        to the claimant and\n\n\n2. deducting, in each benefit week\n\n\n        2.1 any earnings2 (see
        DMG 26001 et seq and 27000 et seq) and\n\n\n        2.2 pension payments3 (see DMG 23800 et seq)."
      locator: DMG 23007
